				name       	"GenerateInstanceInitializer"
				value      	FALSE)
			    (object Attribute
				tool       	"Java"
				name       	"GenerateDefaultConstructor"
				value      	FALSE))
			quid       	"3B2371EA012B"
			documentation 	
|Implements a simple Scanner for an LL(1) Grammar with the basic PASCAL Types:
| * Number, Integer and Hex expressed as long
| * Real expressed as double
| * Identifier, Label as String
| * Character(not enclosed in '')
| * String	(not enclosed in "")
| *
| * A Scanner attributes Meaning to single Characters
| * like Separators, WhiteSpace, Digits etc.
| *
| * This Scanner is made obsolete by Stream.Scanner, although Stream.Scanner
| * works a little bit different by adding the Characters to the Buffer already
| * on calling Character(), while this class only adds it on the next Call!
| * Variables have a single Character and the Multiplication Sign can be skipped.
| * Takes a String as Input and gets the next Character.
| * No Backtracking necessary, because of LL(1).
| * Top-Down Implementation.	 
			
			module     	"Component View::String::Scanner"
			quidu      	"3B2371EA012A"
			language   	"Java")
