				documentation 	
|
|  * MultiplexerIn.java
|  * The MultiplexerIn is in Fact a DeMultiplexer
|  * and derived from the abstract Base Class AStreamIn
|  * and multiplexes the Stream to a List of Output Streams in a Round Robin Fashion.
|  * Instead of appending an (infinite) Number of finite Input Streams
|  * like in 'Union' this interleaves a fixed Number of (infinite) Input Streams.
|  * Any StreamIn can also be used as a DeMultiplexer
|  * by just connecting several Processes, Threads etc. to it
|  *
|  * Created on 26. Mai 2001, 22:08
|  *
|  * @author  Matthias Heuer
|  * @version
|  
				
