						type       	"long"))
					concurrency 	"Sequential"
					opExportControl 	"Protected"
					uid        	0)
				    (object Operation "available"
					attributes 	(list Attribute_Set)
					quid       	"3B2371EE00A9"
					documentation 	
|Returns the (minimum) Number of Items left (in the Buffer).
| * The actual Number may be higher, so available() should be called again
| * at the End of this Number.
| *
| * Nearly equivalent is currItem != null
| * (when the Container does not contain null Entries, like e.g. HashTables)
| 
					
					result     	"long"
					concurrency 	"Sequential"
					opExportControl 	"Public"
					uid        	0)
				    (object Operation "nextItem"
					attributes 	(list Attribute_Set)
					quid       	"3B2371EE00AA"
					documentation 	
|Returns the next (Parent) Object of this one.
| * No Exception is thrown at the End, instead EOI is returned.
| * When IO Processes are bound to this Stream, IOException is wrapped into an IOError.
| * This is less explicit, but much faster because Exception Handling can be extremely slow.
| * Alternatively this Method can block until new Data is available,
| * but this should always have a TimeOut to avoid DeadLocks.
| 
					
					result     	"Object"
					concurrency 	"Sequential"
					opExportControl 	"Public"
					uid        	0)
				    (object Operation "Iterator"
					attributes 	(list Attribute_Set)
					quid       	"3B2371EE00AB"
					documentation 	
| Returns a new Input Stream of the Objects in this Container
|  * in exactly the same State as this one.
|  * If this Container does not support multiple concurrent Iterators, returns 'null'
|  *
|  * Reference to the ByRefChar would stay the same,
|  * that's why you cannot simply use clone().
|  *
|  * @return  a new Input Stream of the Objects in this Container.
|  * @see     Math.Iterator     
					
					result     	"IStreamIn"
					concurrency 	"Sequential"
					opExportControl 	"Public"
					uid        	0)
				    (object Operation "isMonotonous"
					attributes 	(list Attribute_Set)
					quid       	"3B2371EE00AC"
					documentation 	
| @return true, when the Items returned support the OrderAble Interface
|  * and they are returned in (strictly) ascending Order.
|  * This is used as a criterion for Search Operations like findFirst()	 
					
					result     	"boolean"
					concurrency 	"Sequential"
					opExportControl 	"Public"
					uid        	0)
				    (object Operation "currItem"
					attributes 	(list Attribute_Set)
					quid       	"3B2371EE00AD"
					documentation 	
|Returns the current Object that was returned from the last nextItem() Method.	 
					
					result     	"Object"
					concurrency 	"Sequential"
					opExportControl 	"Public"
					uid        	0)
				    (object Operation "skip"
					attributes 	(list Attribute_Set)
					quid       	"3B2371EE00AE"
					documentation 	
|Skips over and discards n Items from this Iterator.
| * Returns the actual number of bytes skipped.
| * This dumb Implementation just reads all Elements and discards them.	 
					
					parameters 	(list Parameters
					    (object Parameter "Position"
						type       	"long"))
					result     	"long"
					concurrency 	"Sequential"
					opExportControl 	"Public"
					uid        	0)
				    (object Operation "reset"
					attributes 	(list Attribute_Set)
					quid       	"3B2371EE00B0"
					documentation 	
|Resets the Iterator to the given Position
| * counted from the last marked Position.	 
					
					parameters 	(list Parameters
					    (object Parameter "Position"
						type       	"long"))
					result     	"void"
					exceptions 	"OperationNotSupported"
					concurrency 	"Sequential"
					opExportControl 	"Public"
					uid        	0)
				    (object Operation "mark"
					attributes 	(list Attribute_Set)
					quid       	"3B2371EE00B2"
					documentation 	
|Marks the current position in this Iterator.
| * A subsequent call to the reset method repositions this Iterator
| * at the last marked position.
| * The readlimit arguments tells this input stream to allow that many Items
| * to be read before the mark position gets invalidated.
| * This is to limit the Blocking of System Ressources	 
					
					parameters 	(list Parameters
					    (object Parameter "ReadLimit"
						type       	"long"))
					result     	"void"
					exceptions 	"OperationNotSupported"
					concurrency 	"Sequential"
					opExportControl 	"Public"
					uid        	0)
